# =============================================================================
# Secret material that lives ONLY on the deployment host — never commit it.
# =============================================================================
# nginx/ssl/ holds the TLS private key AND .htpasswd (the closed-beta password
# hash). It is mounted read-only into the nginx container from the host. It was
# not previously ignored, so a `git add -A` on a host that has this directory
# would have committed the private key and the password hash.
nginx/ssl/
**/.htpasswd
*.pem
!paper/**/*.pem

# The receipt signing key, if ever written to disk (see .env.example).
receipt_private.pem
*.key
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- BMC submission working files: deliberately NOT tracked -------------------
# The letterhead cover letter carries the LIVE reviewer password. This repo is
# public and is archived to Zenodo on every release, so committing it would
# publish the credential to everyone. The tracked source of truth is
# paper/bmc_bioinformatics/cover_letter.md, which keeps a [REVIEWER-PASSWORD]
# placeholder; the real value is substituted only in the copy uploaded to the
# portal, and lives on the host in /root/stickforstats-beta-access.txt.
paper/bmc_bioinformatics/Cover-letter-BMC-Bioinformatics.doc
# The release source archive: 62 MB, already published at
# https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21797621, and reproducible from the v1.2.0 tag.
paper/bmc_bioinformatics/stickforstats_new-v*.zip
